## 6. Compliance

| ID | Requirement | Testable Criterion | Status (2026-07-07) |
|----|-------------|-------------------|---------------------|
| CXC-BE-C1 | Visual attribute binding | Bind an attribute to a namespace via the picker/drag, zero YAML typed → exported `.compose.yaml` carries the binding | PASS — picker Save → `composer/config/widget_changed` → raw spec → export (test_c1; MQTT smoke: a REMOTE Intelligence binds the same way) |
| CXC-BE-C2 | Visual behavior config | Configure a `blink`/`rotate` via the UI (trigger + params) → the previewed widget exhibits it | PASS — WW preview wires attr_bindings + behaviors to the design bus/host BehaviorEngine; blink measured [on,off,on,off] at half-periods; revert-on-release holds in preview |
| CXC-BE-C3 | Introspection-driven UI | Behaviors/attrs/param-fields come from engine tables; a new engine behavior appears with no editor code change | PASS — schema covers all 7 behaviors; injected "wobble" row surfaces its param field untouched |
| CXC-BE-C4 | Source sync | Canvas edit → Source updates; Source edit → canvas updates; selection is linked both ways | PASS — both directions incl. flow-style one-line mappings; remote source/replace over MQTT projects too |
| CXC-BE-C5 | Edit safety | An invalid Source edit shows an inline error and does not alter the visual state | PASS — commit only on valid parse; error line highlighted + status bar + `composer/source/status` on the bus; document byte-unchanged |
| CXC-BE-C6 | Pop-out | Source opens full-width in its own window and stays synced | PASS — full-width DialogWidget (1380px panel), second SourcePanel over the same document; edit in pop-out syncs the docked view; 0-px identical macOS↔RPi5 |
| CXC-BE-C7 | Raw-spec fidelity | A design with bindings/variables/behaviors round-trips through the editor with no lossy re-serialization | PASS — byte-identical incl. bare-string visible, object bindings, literal maps, `$var` params, `is_exact`, doc-level `variables:`; 3 fidelity gaps found+closed (see [CXC-BE-RAWSPEC]) |
| CXC-BE-C8 | DSL-candidate capture | Reaching for arithmetic logs a use-case candidate rather than accepting inline code | PASS — refused + jsonl-logged + bus event; explicit "log it" affordance; heuristic spares URIs/hex colors |

